# Illustrative semantic data contract for the GrainCorp elevation-capacity table ([[R211]],
# spec 2026-09-11-the-span-the-author-drew-design.md § 3.3).
#
# FOUR FIELDS, AND DELIBERATELY NO FIELD FOR THE FLAG. The page prints, per port, a tonnage and
# a Y/N. `capacity` declares the numeral pattern, so 'Y' and 'N' fail the value constraint and
# QUARANTINE — which is the second half of the maintainer's Split ruling, and it falls out of
# the membrane with no special case. Naming the flag would mean asserting what Y/N MEANS, and
# nothing on the page says (spec § 6). `Available` and `On Application` quarantine the same way:
# they describe availability, not a tonnage.
#
# `port` IS SCHEME-BOUND, and that is what makes the key split groundable. The spanning header's
# labels reach the portal as split keys — text that IS its value — which `exact_field` can never
# place; `marker_field` grounds them by UNIQUE admission to ship:scheme-port instead.
#
# `year` and `elevationPeriod` are the two columns NO spanning header covers, so every split
# record carries them, and their column labels name them exactly — they ground by exact field
# match and need no scheme.
#
# WHAT IS NOT DECLARED HERE, and why the omission is the honest one: a provenance pointer naming
# the furniture the measure's NAME was derived from (plan DECISION G). The maintainer's ruling
# (§ 0) is that the MACHINE derives that name from the page's title and footer, and the path that
# carries it to the proposer is not yet built. The pointer's target is also document-scoped — the
# ignored band's source region is minted per compiled document URI — so a contract file cannot
# name it without asserting an identity it cannot know. It belongs with the loop that hands the
# proposer the page, not with this one.
@prefix ship: <https://example.org/shipping#> .
@prefix etkl: <https://w3id.org/iladub/etkl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

ship:capacity-contract a etkl:SemanticDataContract ;
    rdfs:label "Elevation capacity, by port and period"@en ;
    etkl:targetClass ship:ElevationCapacity ;
    etkl:requiresKnowledge ship:scheme-port ;
    etkl:hasField ship:f-cap-year , ship:f-cap-period , ship:f-cap-port , ship:f-cap-capacity .

ship:f-cap-year     a etkl:Field ; etkl:fillsProperty ship:year .
ship:f-cap-period   a etkl:Field ; etkl:fillsProperty ship:elevationPeriod .
ship:f-cap-port     a etkl:Field ; etkl:fillsProperty ship:port ; etkl:admissibleScheme ship:scheme-port .
ship:f-cap-capacity a etkl:Field ; etkl:fillsProperty ship:capacity .
